                <pb facs="0869" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-06T10:00:00-05:00">March 6, 1929—10
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Your 27, March 3, noon. I very much hope that the Government of Chile will
                    not permit the question of the erection of the monument on the Morro or the
                    expense of the port to stand in the way of a definitive settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
